    "code": "def solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    advertising_expenditure = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]\n    monthly_sales_revenue = [15, 30, 50, 40, 65]\n\n    # Do math calculation to get the answer\n    n = len(advertising_expenditure)\n    mean_x = sum(advertising_expenditure) / n\n    mean_y = sum(monthly_sales_revenue) / n\n\n    numerator = sum(\n        (x - mean_x) * (y - mean_y)\n        for x, y in zip(advertising_expenditure, monthly_sales_revenue)\n    )\n    denominator = sum(\n        (x - mean_x) ** 2\n        for x in advertising_expenditure\n    )\n\n    slope = numerator / denominator\n\n    # return answer\n    return round(slope, 2)\n"
